        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="policy-meta">
          <strong>Effective date:</strong> 17 June 2026<br />
          <strong>Public URL (Google Play, AdMob, App Store):</strong>
          <a href="https://unrecorded.app/privacy">https://unrecorded.app/privacy</a>
              (also reachable at
              <a href="https://unrecorded.app/privacy.html"
                >https://unrecorded.app/privacy.html</a
              >)
        </p>

        <p>
          Unrecorded is a privacy awareness app created by Meldlife Ltd.
        </p>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Unrecorded handles information when you
          use the Unrecorded app or visit the Unrecorded website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unrecorded is designed to be <strong>local-first</strong>. The app scans
          nearby Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) signals for patterns that may indicate
          smart glasses or wearable recording devices. Detection and risk scoring run
          on your device. Nearby Bluetooth scan results are
          <strong>not uploaded</strong> to Meldlife Ltd or other servers we operate.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Unrecorded does not prove that anyone is recording.</strong> It shows
          <em>possible</em> privacy risk indicators (for example low, medium, or high
          risk) based on nearby signals visible to your device. Alerts and notifications
          describe possible risk — not confirmed recording.
        </p>

        <div class="policy-summary" role="region" aria-label="App privacy summary">
          <p><strong>At a glance (app):</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>BLE scanning and risk scoring are processed on your device</li>
            <li>Nearby scan data is not uploaded to us</li>
            <li>No account required; no analytics or telemetry in the core app</li>
            <li>Official store builds may show Google AdMob banner ads; optional pay-what-you-want in-app purchase to remove ads</li>
            <li>Scan results and nearby device identifiers are not passed to ad networks</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2 id="who">1. Who We Are</h2>
        <p>
          Unrecorded is operated by <strong>Meldlife Ltd</strong> (“MeldLife”, “we”,
          “us”, “our”).
        </p>
        <p>
          For this policy: “Unrecorded”, “we”, “us”, and “our” refer to Meldlife Ltd
          and the Unrecorded app.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy enquiries:
          <a href="mailto:privacy@unrecorded.app">privacy@unrecorded.app</a>
        </p>

        <h2 id="summary">2. Summary</h2>
        <p>Unrecorded is designed to minimise data collection.</p>
        <div class="policy-summary">
          <p><strong>The app:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>does not require an account</li>
            <li>
              processes Bluetooth Low Energy scanning and privacy risk scoring on your
              device (local-first)
            </li>
            <li>
              does not upload nearby Bluetooth scan results to our servers
            </li>
            <li>
              does not include third-party analytics or telemetry
            </li>
            <li>does not use scan data to identify you</li>
            <li>does not build a profile about you</li>
            <li>does not tell us who or what is near you</li>
            <li>
              shows possible privacy risk indicators — it does not prove whether anyone
              is recording
            </li>
            <li>
              may show small banner ads via Google AdMob in official app-store builds
              (see section 7)
            </li>
            <li>
              offers an optional in-app purchase to remove ads; core scanning stays free
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p>
          The app processes nearby signal information on your device so it can show
          possible privacy risk indicators. Wording in the app is intentionally cautious:
          signals may <em>match</em> known patterns; that is not proof of recording.
        </p>

        <h2 id="app-data">3. Information Processed by the App (Bluetooth / BLE)</h2>
        <p>
          When you use Unrecorded, the app processes nearby Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)
          signal information made available by your device and operating system. This
          happens <strong>on your device</strong> to evaluate possible privacy risk — not
          to prove that recording is taking place.
        </p>
        <p>This may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>visible Bluetooth device names</li>
          <li>Bluetooth identifiers made available by the operating system</li>
          <li>approximate signal strength</li>
          <li>whether a nearby device appears connectable</li>
          <li>signal patterns or indicators used by the app’s risk model</li>
          <li>risk level and explanation shown in the app</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This information is used to help the app identify signals that may match
          smart glasses or wearable recording devices.
        </p>
        <p>
          Bluetooth identifiers and visible names can be hidden, randomised, spoofed,
          or inaccurate. Signal strength is noisy and should not be treated as a
          precise distance measurement.
        </p>

        <h2 id="on-device">4. What Stays on Your Device</h2>
        <p>
          Unrecorded is designed so nearby BLE scan data stays on your device. All
          detection and scoring for privacy risk indicators is performed locally.
        </p>
        <p>
          Meldlife Ltd does not collect, receive, or upload your nearby Bluetooth scan
          results, device names seen during scans, or risk scores derived from those
          scans.
        </p>
        <p>We do not use nearby scan data to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>identify you</li>
          <li>track your location</li>
          <li>track people around you</li>
          <li>build an advertising profile</li>
          <li>sell information about you</li>
          <li>monitor your behaviour</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="accounts">5. Accounts</h2>
        <p>Unrecorded does not require you to create an account.</p>

        <h2 id="analytics">6. Analytics and Core App Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The core Unrecorded experience — Bluetooth scanning, risk scoring, and privacy
          alerts — does not include third-party analytics or telemetry.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ad serving in official store builds uses Google AdMob (see section 7). AdMob
          may collect or process data according to Google’s policies; that is separate
          from our BLE scan pipeline.
        </p>

        <h2 id="ads">7. Advertising (Google AdMob) and In-App Purchases</h2>

        <h3>Advertising — Google AdMob</h3>
        <p>
          Official Google Play and other app-store builds of Unrecorded may display
          small bottom <strong>banner advertisements</strong> served by
          <strong>Google AdMob</strong> on some screens (for example when no active
          privacy alert is shown, and on help or settings screens). Ads are optional to
          remove via in-app purchase (below).
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Isolation from scanning:</strong> The detection engine and scan logic
            do not depend on advertising, analytics, or cloud tracking. Ad code is kept
            separate from Bluetooth scanning and risk scoring.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No scan data to ads:</strong> Nearby Bluetooth scan results, visible
            device names, Bluetooth identifiers, and privacy risk outputs are
            <strong>not</strong> passed to AdMob or other ad networks.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Non-personalised ads only:</strong> All ad requests use
            non-personalised ads. Unrecorded does not enable personalised advertising.
            Where required (for example UK / GDPR), Google’s User Messaging Platform
            (UMP) may ask for your advertising consent and provide a way to change or
            withdraw those choices.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Device advertising identifiers:</strong> Official store builds use the
            device advertising identifier required by Google AdMob and app-store policy
            (for example the Android advertising ID). That identifier is used only for ad
            serving through AdMob — not for Bluetooth scanning, risk scoring, or building
            a profile from nearby devices.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Change your choices:</strong> In the app, open
            <strong>Settings &amp; Privacy → Ad privacy choices</strong> to change or
            withdraw advertising consent where UMP applies.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>What AdMob may process:</strong> When an ad is shown, Google AdMob may
            still process limited information — such as advertising ID, IP address, device
            type, and interaction with ads — for ad delivery, fraud prevention, and
            reporting, even when ads are non-personalised, as described in
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Google’s Privacy Policy</a
            >
            and
            <a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >Google’s information about how AdMob uses data</a
            >. You can limit ad personalisation in your device settings where available.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>In-app purchase — remove ads</h3>
        <p>
          Unrecorded offers an optional <strong>pay-what-you-want</strong>
          non-consumable in-app purchase to remove banner ads. Core Bluetooth scanning and
          privacy risk indicators remain free.
        </p>
        <p>
          Purchases are processed by the app store you use (for example
          <strong>Google Play Billing</strong> on Android or
          <strong>Apple In-App Purchase</strong> on iOS). Meldlife Ltd does not receive your
          full payment card details. The store may process purchase history, account
          identifiers, and region according to its own privacy policy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ad-free entitlement is stored <strong>locally on your device</strong>. Meldlife
          Ltd does not operate a separate purchase or receipt server. You can
          <strong>restore purchases</strong> through the app or your app-store account to
          re-enable ad-free access on a new device or after reinstalling.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open-source builds of Unrecorded remain available to build from source under the
          project licence; those builds may omit store ads and billing unless you configure
          them yourself.
        </p>

        <h2 id="permissions">8. Permissions</h2>
        <p>
          Unrecorded may request Bluetooth, nearby device, notification, or
          location-related permissions depending on your device and operating system.
        </p>
        <p>
          These permissions are used so the app can scan nearby Bluetooth signals and
          show relevant privacy risk indicators.
        </p>
        <p>
          On some versions of Android or iOS, Bluetooth scanning may require
          permissions that sound broader than Unrecorded’s actual use. Unrecorded uses
          these permissions for nearby signal awareness, not to track your physical
          location.
        </p>
        <p>Permission behaviour may differ between Android and iOS.</p>
        <p>
          On Android store builds, Google AdMob may use the device advertising identifier
          and related ad SDK permissions for banner ads only (see section 7). That is
          separate from Bluetooth scan permissions and does not give ads access to
          nearby-device scan results.
        </p>
        <p>You can control app permissions through your device settings.</p>

        <h2 id="notifications">9. Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          If you enable notifications, Unrecorded uses them to show app status or privacy
          risk alerts. Notifications describe possible risk — not confirmed recording.
        </p>
        <p>You can disable notifications through your device settings.</p>

        <h2 id="website">10. Website Privacy</h2>
        <p>The Unrecorded website is a simple static site.</p>
        <p>The website does not use:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>cookies</li>
          <li>analytics scripts</li>
          <li>tracking pixels</li>
          <li>behavioural advertising scripts</li>
          <li>browser fingerprinting</li>
          <li>unnecessary third-party embeds</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If the hosting provider collects basic server logs for security, reliability,
          or abuse prevention, those logs are controlled by the hosting provider.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cannot-do">11. What Unrecorded Cannot Do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Unrecorded cannot confirm that someone is recording.</li>
          <li>
            Unrecorded cannot detect every camera, microphone, phone, or recording
            device.
          </li>
          <li>
            Unrecorded cannot guarantee that a nearby signal belongs to smart glasses.
          </li>
          <li>
            Unrecorded cannot detect devices that do not expose useful Bluetooth
            signals.
          </li>
          <li>Unrecorded cannot prevent recording.</li>
          <li>
            Unrecorded should be treated as a privacy awareness tool, not a security
            guarantee.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="retention">12. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Because Unrecorded processes scan information locally on your device, we do not
          retain nearby Bluetooth scan results on our servers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Scan state used for alerts is held on your device and cleared when you delete
          app data or uninstall the app.
        </p>

        <h2 id="sharing">13. Sharing Information</h2>
        <p>We do not sell your Bluetooth scan data.</p>
        <p>
          We do not share nearby Bluetooth scan results, device names from scans, or risk
          scores with advertisers, data brokers, or third-party analytics providers.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information may be processed by third parties only where necessary for services
          such as:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Google AdMob</strong> — banner advertising in official store builds
            (see section 7; scan data is not shared with AdMob)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Play</strong> or <strong>Apple App Store</strong> — app
            distribution and in-app purchase processing
          </li>
          <li>website hosting for <code>unrecorded.app</code></li>
          <li>security and abuse prevention by infrastructure providers</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="children">14. Children</h2>
        <p>
          Unrecorded is not directed at children and is intended as a general privacy
          awareness tool for adults.
        </p>

        <h2 id="international">15. International Processing</h2>
        <p>
          If you visit the website or install the app through an app store, some
          information may be processed by infrastructure providers, app stores, payment
          providers, or hosting providers in other countries.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where this applies, those providers are responsible for their own processing
          under their own privacy policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unrecorded itself does not upload nearby scan results to our servers.
        </p>

        <h2 id="rights">16. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may have rights over personal information,
          such as the right to ask for access, correction, deletion, or restriction of
          processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because Unrecorded does not require an account and does not upload nearby scan
          results to our servers, we may not hold personal information that identifies you.
        </p>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or requests, contact
          <a href="mailto:privacy@unrecorded.app">privacy@unrecorded.app</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="opensource">17. Open-Source Project</h2>
        <p>Unrecorded is an open-source project.</p>
        <p>
          This helps users and contributors inspect how the app works, understand its
          limitations, and suggest improvements.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open-source transparency does not change the privacy commitments described in
          this policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">18. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time.</p>
        <p>
          When we make meaningful changes, we will update the effective date above and
          publish the revised policy at this URL.
        </p>

